            "number": 1593,
            "title": "docs(static): fix route path in serveStatic example to match root access",
            "body": "Fixes #1578.\n\nIn `docs/4.examples/serve-static-assets.md`, the text explains:\n\n> Now, create a `index.html` file in the `public` directory with a simple message and open your browser to http://localhost:3000. You should see the message.\n\nMounting the handler under `app.use(\"/public/**\", ...)` causes:\n1. Requests to `http://localhost:3000` return a 404 because they do not match `/public/**`.\n2. Even when requesting `http://localhost:3000/public/index.html`, `id` is passed as `/public/index.html`, and `path.join(\"public\", id)` resolves to `public/public/index.html`.\n\nUpdating the route path in the code examples to `app.use(\"/**\", ...)` aligns the example with the documented instructions and the test patterns in `test/static.test.ts`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated both static-asset examples to serve requests from the root path instead of only under `/public`.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
